{"type": "tool_call", "n": 64, "ts": 1790151539.4622579, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US OPERATING EXPENSE FLUX \u2014 MARCH 2026 vs FEBRUARY 2026 (USD)\nPrepared 2026-04-03 by David Murguia (david.murguia@gmail.com)\n\nSTATUS: PARTIAL. I hit the 60-call tool budget after pulling all account balances and the detail for Hosting and Feb Travel. March Travel and Feb/Mar Marketing detail were NOT retrieved, so those two drivers are unverified. No entries were posted and no exceptions were logged through the tool (budget exhausted); items needing follow-up are listed in Section 4.\n\n1. FLUX TABLE (period activity, debit minus credit)\nAcct  Name                        Feb 2026     Mar 2026     Change      %       Flag\n5000  Hosting & Infrastructure    31,301.80    40,948.20   +9,646.40   +30.8%  EXPLAIN\n6000  Salaries & Wages           183,800.38   184,465.91     +665.53    +0.4%  \u2014\n6010  Payroll Taxes               14,060.73    14,111.64      +50.91    +0.4%  \u2014\n6100  Rent                        14,500.00    14,500.00        0.00     0.0%  \u2014\n6110  Utilities                      919.82       922.22       +2.40    +0.3%  \u2014\n6200  Software Subscriptions       4,139.80     3,339.50     -800.30   -19.3%  >10% but <$5k\n6300  Travel                         785.40     7,158.41   +6,373.01  +811.4%  EXPLAIN\n6310  Meals & Entertainment          114.32        49.75      -64.57   -56.5%  <$5k\n6320  Training & Conferences         542.56         0.00     -542.56  -100.0%  <$5k\n6400  Marketing Programs           7,898.14    29,686.00  +21,787.86  +275.9%  EXPLAIN\n6600  Office Supplies                197.75       281.47      +83.72   +42.3%  <$5k\n6800  Depreciation                 3,425.00         0.00   -3,425.00  -100.0%  <$5k \u2014 see 4(c)\n6900  Bank Fees                       65.00         0.00      -65.00  -100.0%  <$5k \u2014 see 4(d)\nAll other expense accounts (5100, 5200, 6020, 6030, 6120, 6410, 6500, 6510, 6520, 6550, 6700, 6950, 7000, 7100, 7200): zero activity in both months.\nTotal opex incl. hosting: Feb 261,750.70 \u2192 Mar 295,483.10, +33,732.40 (+12.9%).\n\n2. LINES OVER BOTH THRESHOLDS (>10% AND >$5,000)\n\n(a) 5000 Hosting & Infrastructure: +9,646.40 (+30.8%) \u2014 DRIVER VERIFIED AT LEDGER LEVEL\n  Feb: JE-00125 (2026-02-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-12523, cloud infrastructure \u2013 production, 31,301.80 (AP, support attached).\n  Mar: JE-00232 (2026-03-03) Stackline Cloud inv STA-98877, cloud infrastructure \u2013 production, 31,148.20 (AP, support attached) \u2014 recurring charge, down 153.60 vs Feb.\n       JE-00258 (2026-03-14) Stackline Cloud inv SC-M-2203, \"one-time data migration\", 9,800.00 (AP, support attached).\n  Reconciliation of the move: +9,800.00 (one-time migration) \u2013 153.60 (recurring run-rate) = +9,646.40. Ties exactly.\n  Caveat / does it hold up: The recurring piece is clean. The 9,800 is described as one-time, so March hosting is not the new run-rate; expect ~31.1k in April. I could not open SC-M-2203 to confirm the invoice text, service period, or whether any portion is a capitalizable implementation cost vs. period expense. Recommend the controller review the invoice before accepting 5000 as the final classification.\n\n(b) 6300 Travel: +6,373.01 (+811%) \u2014 DRIVER NOT VERIFIED\n  Feb detail (785.40, all card, support attached): JE-00132 Uber 31.36; JE-00167 Delta airfare 420.62; JE-00188 Uber 38.32; JE-00196 Hilton Garden Inn 295.10.\n  Mar detail (7,158.41): NOT RETRIEVED \u2014 budget exhausted. I cannot cite the March transactions or say whether the increase is genuine trip volume, a single large booking, a miscoding, or an accrual. Treat this line as open.\n\n(c) 6400 Marketing Programs: +21,787.86 (+276%) \u2014 DRIVER NOT VERIFIED\n  Feb detail (7,898.14) and Mar detail (29,686.00): NOT RETRIEVED. The March figure is a round 29,686.00 with no cents, which is consistent with invoice- or accrual-driven activity rather than card spend, but that is an inference, not evidence. Treat this line as open; it is the largest single mover in the month.\n\n3. OTHER OBSERVATIONS (below threshold)\n  - 6200 Software Subscriptions down 800.30 (-19%): below the $5k bar; not investigated.\n  - 6320 Training and 6310 Meals down to near zero: immaterial.\n\n4. ITEMS NEEDING CONTROLLER FOLLOW-UP (could not be flagged via tool \u2014 budget exhausted)\n  (a) Pull March 6300 Travel detail (7,158.41) and identify drivers; confirm receipts/support.\n  (b) Pull Feb and March 6400 Marketing detail (7,898.14 / 29,686.00) and identify drivers; confirm invoices/support and service periods (possible prepaid or accrual-timing element).\n  (c) 6800 Depreciation is 0.00 in March vs 3,425.00 in each of Jan and Feb (YTD balance unchanged at 6,850.00). The March depreciation entry appears not to have been posted. Not part of the >$5k flux, but it is a likely missing close entry and will understate March opex by ~3,425 until booked. I did not post it \u2014 no fixed-asset schedule was reviewed.\n  (d) 6900 Bank Fees 0.00 in March vs 65.00 in Jan and Feb: March bank fee probably not yet recorded (immaterial, but check the bank statement during the cash rec).\n  (e) Review Stackline SC-M-2203 (JE-00258, 9,800.00) for classification (expense vs. capitalizable) and confirm it is genuinely non-recurring.\n\n5. ACTIONS TAKEN\n  None. No journal entries posted, no reversals, no bank matches, no checklist items changed.\n\nBottom line: Hosting is explained and ties to the penny (one-time 9,800 Stackline migration invoice). Travel and Marketing \u2014 28.2k of the 33.7k total increase \u2014 are NOT explained in this memo because I ran out of tool calls before pulling their detail; they should not be signed off until someone does. Depreciation for March looks unposted."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
